1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,701
This video puts the entire syllabus on one page.

2
00:00:03,701 --> 00:00:15,960
We walk through the complete exploratory data analysis workflow, from the first question to the final insight, and show which lecture and lab covers each step.

3
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:18,416
Steps one to four.

4
00:00:18,416 --> 00:00:19,244
Step one:

5
00:00:19,244 --> 00:00:22,095
frame the problem and the data:

6
00:00:22,095 --> 00:00:28,351
what is a row, what is the outcome, and what can the sample support?

7
00:00:28,351 --> 00:00:29,178
Step two:

8
00:00:29,178 --> 00:00:30,558
audit the data:

9
00:00:30,558 --> 00:00:35,618
shape, types, missing values, duplicates, hidden zeros.

10
00:00:35,618 --> 00:00:36,630
Step three:

11
00:00:36,630 --> 00:00:40,033
understand data types and structures.

12
00:00:40,033 --> 00:00:40,953
Step four:

13
00:00:40,953 --> 00:00:43,069
describe distributions:

14
00:00:43,069 --> 00:00:48,680
centre, spread, shape, with median and I Q R for skewed data.

15
00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:51,320
Steps five to eight.

16
00:00:51,320 --> 00:00:52,241
Step five:

17
00:00:52,241 --> 00:01:03,099
explore relationships with correlation, cross-tabs and grouped statistics, and discover groups with V I F and K-Means.

18
00:01:03,099 --> 00:01:03,928
Step six:

19
00:01:03,928 --> 00:01:07,425
visualise honestly and tell the story.

20
00:01:07,425 --> 00:01:08,437
Step seven:

21
00:01:08,437 --> 00:01:10,001
fix data quality:

22
00:01:10,001 --> 00:01:14,786
integration, duplicates, encoding, validation rules.

23
00:01:14,786 --> 00:01:15,799
Step eight:

24
00:01:15,799 --> 00:01:21,136
handle missing values and outliers by mechanism and cause.

25
00:01:21,936 --> 00:01:23,807
Steps nine to twelve.

26
00:01:23,807 --> 00:01:24,697
Step nine:

27
00:01:24,697 --> 00:01:28,171
encode categories and handle imbalance.

28
00:01:28,171 --> 00:01:28,973
Step ten:

29
00:01:28,973 --> 00:01:33,783
transform and scale, and engineer and select features.

30
00:01:33,783 --> 00:01:34,852
Step eleven:

31
00:01:34,852 --> 00:01:44,205
reduce dimensions with P C A, and test honestly with a stratified split, cross-validation and no leakage.

32
00:01:44,205 --> 00:01:45,274
Step twelve:

33
00:01:45,274 --> 00:01:54,360
translate results into insights as observation, evidence, meaning and action, with limitations stated.

34
00:01:55,160 --> 00:01:58,087
Four ideas run through every step.

35
00:01:58,087 --> 00:02:03,683
Plot and compute together, since each hides what the other shows.

36
00:02:03,683 --> 00:02:05,663
Ask why before you fix:

37
00:02:05,663 --> 00:02:08,848
why is it missing, why is it extreme.

38
00:02:08,848 --> 00:02:12,722
Never let the test data influence any choice:

39
00:02:12,722 --> 00:02:16,338
split first and fit on training rows only.

40
00:02:16,338 --> 00:02:18,060
And report honestly:

41
00:02:18,060 --> 00:02:25,808
label exploratory against confirmatory, state limits, and say what the data cannot answer.

42
00:02:26,608 --> 00:02:28,102
Where to go next.

43
00:02:28,102 --> 00:02:31,706
Re-do every lab on a dataset of your own.

44
00:02:31,706 --> 00:02:35,925
Use the module revision videos to test yourself.

45
00:02:35,925 --> 00:02:41,374
Prepare the assignments and the final project with the guides.

46
00:02:41,374 --> 00:02:45,769
And read the textbooks in the course reading list.

47
00:02:45,769 --> 00:02:51,130
You now have the complete exploratory data analysis workflow.

48
00:02:51,130 --> 00:02:52,888
Thanks for watching.

